<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Company rule in Rhodesia</h1><p class="st-meta">1890 CE – 1923 CE · capital Salisbury</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The era when Cecil Rhodes's British South Africa Company governed the lands that became Zimbabwe and Zambia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1889 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-rhodes">Cecil Rhodes</a> received a royal charter, based on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudd-concession">Rudd Concession</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lobengula">Lobengula</a>. Its Pioneer Column marched into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mashonaland">Mashonaland</a> and raised the flag at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harare">Fort Salisbury</a> in September 1890. In 1893 the company conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele Kingdom</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The company ruled through administrators such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leander-starr-jameson">Leander Starr Jameson</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-milton">William Milton</a>, granting land and mining claims to settlers in hope of a second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/witwatersrand">Witwatersrand</a> that never appeared. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shona">Shona</a> risings of 1896-1897, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-chimurenga">first Chimurenga</a>, were suppressed. North of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> it governed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-western-rhodesia">North-Western Rhodesia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-eastern-rhodesia">North-Eastern Rhodesia</a>, later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Settlers resented company rule. In a 1922 referendum they rejected union with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-south-africa">South Africa</a>, and in 1923 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/southern-rhodesia">Southern Rhodesia</a> became a self-governing British colony; <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a> passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colonial-office">Colonial Office</a> in 1924, though the company kept mineral rights.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/company-rule-in-rhodesia.jpg" alt="Company rule in Rhodesia" width="320" height="162"><figcaption>Image: Mangwanani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_British_South_Africa_Company.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1890 CE – 1923 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Salisbury</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cecil Rhodes, Leander Starr Jameson, William Milton</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Shona, isiNdebele</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a>, <a href="/countries/zambia">Zambia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British South Africa Company territory, Rhodesia (BSAC), Zambesia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1906&amp;focus=company-rule-in-rhodesia" aria-label="Company rule in Rhodesia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5522 2840 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Company rule in Rhodesia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5842 3096L4997 651M5842 3096L5770 3180M5842 3096L5863 2875M5842 3096L5720 3066M5842 3096L5752 2973M5842 3096L5812 3138"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M5770 3180h0M5863 2875h0M